Add the [build-system] table this sdist is missing.

preprocess_cancellation 0.2.1 ships a pyproject.toml that declares
[tool.poetry] but no [build-system] section at all, and it ships no setup.py
and no setup.cfg. Under PEP 518 the fallback for a pyproject.toml with no
[build-system] is setuptools' legacy backend, which then finds no setup.py and
fails. Declaring the backend the project actually uses is the minimal fix and
changes nothing about the built artifact.

Upstream is unmaintained at this version and Moonraker pins it exactly
(preprocess-cancellation==0.2.1), so bumping to a fixed release is not an
option here.

NOTE: this file uses CRLF line endings upstream; this patch preserves them.

Signed-off-by: NebulaOS build <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/pyproject.toml	2024-01-31 16:27:37.702213300 +0100
+++ b/pyproject.toml	2026-09-27 12:17:20.297479578 +0200
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
+[build-system]
+requires = ["poetry-core>=1.0.0"]
+build-backend = "poetry.core.masonry.api"
+
 [tool.poetry]
 name = "preprocess_cancellation"
 version = "0.2.1"
